- add webhook monitoring and idempotency,
- test failed-payment and refunded-payment scenarios,
- make the app show `Regular` or `Premium` from the backend.

After launch:
- add iOS In-App Purchase,
- add Google Play Billing,
- optionally add RevenueCat if cross-platform subscription sync becomes painful.

8. My final recommendation

If you force me to give one single default answer:
- use Stripe first.

If you force me to give the best strategic answer:
- use Stripe for web/direct Windows if you are starting UK-first,
- use Paddle instead if your real priority is “sell globally fast without tax/compliance headache,”
- use Apple/Google billing for in-app mobile purchases,
- keep entitlement ownership in your backend,
- add PayPal later only if customers actually ask for it.

So the best way is not “PayPal or Stripe everywhere.”
The best way is:
